course: dictionary
lesson: 11456
title: Words for running things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Administration is the work of organising and running a business, school or office. Think of the jobs that keep things working behind the scenes: sending letters, keeping lists and paying bills.
explain: «The school office does the administration, sending letters home and keeping the registers.» Letters, lists and bills are all paperwork and planning, so administration means the organising work that keeps the school running.
explain: The word can also mean the group of people in charge. «The administration decided to close the car park for repairs.» The clue is decided: a group of people made a choice. In the news, «the president's administration» means the government led by a president.
explain: In health, administration means giving medicine to someone. «The nurse began the administration of the medicine at noon.» The clues are nurse and medicine, so it means giving the medicine. Informal speakers shorten it to admin.
fact: Administration means the work of organising and running a place, such as a school, office or business.
fact: «The administration» can mean the group of people who manage an organisation.
fact: In the USA, an administration can mean a government, especially the one led by a president.
fact: In formal language, «administration of medicine» means giving medicine to someone.
fact: The short, informal form is «admin», which means the same kind of organising work.
exercise: «The school office does the administration, sending letters and keeping registers.» What does administration mean here? | A sports game | * The work of organising and running the school | A school trip to the museum | A new classroom
exercise: «The administration decided to close the car park.» What does the administration mean? | A type of bread | A car park | * The group of people who manage the organisation | The weather
exercise: Mum says, «I'm doing the admin tonight: bills and letters.» What does admin mean? | * The paperwork and organising | A type of bird | Going to bed | Cooking dinner
test: «The nurse began the administration of the medicine at noon.» In this sentence, administration means | * Giving the medicine to someone | Making medicine at home | Selling medicine in a shop | Forgetting the medicine
test: «The president's administration passed a new law.» Here administration means | Clothes worn by the president | * The government led by the president | A birthday party | A school office
exam: Which sentence uses administration to mean the work of organising and running an office? | «The river flowed into the sea.» | «She ate her lunch under the tree.» | «He ran fast through the park.» | * «The office administration kept the files tidy and the bills paid.»
